<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The three app shortcuts on a long press of the icon. MASTER_BUILD_PROMPT 13.5,
    design-v3.md 12.4, Addendum 01 6i, issue #40.

    ## Static, and that is the whole design

    **Three shortcuts, declared here, in this order, forever.** No dynamic shortcuts,
    no pinned shortcuts, no recents, and nothing that reorders itself. 13.5 gives the
    reason and it is not a shrug: a list that rearranged itself around what somebody
    did most would be a measurement of that person, taken without being asked for and
    shown back to them every time they reached for the icon. This app does not do that
    anywhere else and it does not start here.

    A static list is also the only kind that exists **before the app has ever been
    opened**, which is what makes `Quick capture` reachable on the day it is installed.

    ## They are the androidx.core form

    13.5 asks for the androidx.core shortcuts APIs. This file is what those APIs read:
    `ShortcutManagerCompat.getShortcuts(context, FLAG_MATCH_MANIFEST)` parses this
    resource, and the compat library's own pre-26 pinning path parses it too. There is
    no androidx entry point that publishes a shortcut without making it dynamic, so the
    two halves of that sentence are met the only way they can both be met at once.

    ## Every intent here is explicit, and the package name is a resource

    `targetPackage` and `targetClass` together make each intent explicit, so a shortcut
    can only ever reach this app's own Activity and no filter has to be opened on
    `MainActivity` for anything outside the app to match.

    **`@string/clarity_application_id` rather than a literal**, because the debug
    variant is `com.kamsiob.claritynow.debug` and a resource file is one of the few
    places `${applicationId}` does not reach: manifest placeholders are substituted in
    the manifest and nowhere else. The string is generated per build type in
    `app/build.gradle.kts` from the same constant that sets `applicationId`, so the
    suffix is written once. A literal here would have shipped three shortcuts that do
    nothing on every debug install, which is the build every device check runs on.

    ## The three actions are the app's existing ones

    Each shortcut sends the action the matching notification or widget already sends,
    so a destination has one way in rather than two. `ShortcutContractTest` asserts the
    three strings below still equal the three constants they were copied from, because
    an action string in XML is a copy and a copy is a thing that goes stale quietly.

    Quick capture sends `WidgetIntents.ACTION_CAPTURE_UNFILED`, which the add sheet with
    no area answers. Start focus sends `FocusIntents.ACTION_OPEN_FOCUS`, which the Focus
    surface answers. Today's Pulse sends `PulseIntents.ACTION_OPEN_PULSE`, which the Pulse
    sheet answers. There is no table here because an XML comment may not contain two
    dashes in a row, which is also why nothing anywhere in this file is written as one.

    **`Start focus` opens the chooser rather than starting a session**, which is the
    choice #40 leaves to the builder under design-v3.md 15. The obvious answer is to
    start one when exactly one area has an active item, and it is rejected: a session
    is a write to a log that only ever gains rows, and a person who long pressed an
    icon has not yet seen anything. It also keeps the three launcher surfaces saying
    one thing, since the First Step widget asks for a session rather than appending
    `FOCUS_STARTED` from outside a screen. While a session is already running the same
    action opens that session, because the Focus surface shows what the log holds.

    **`Today's Pulse` generates nothing.** The action opens the Pulse surface in
    whatever state the day is in, including the ambient state of a day the engine
    stayed silent on. Generation is the lifecycle's, MASTER_BUILD_PROMPT 11.3, and it
    happens on foreground before any of this is reached.
-->
<shortcuts xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <shortcut
        android:enabled="true"
        android:icon="@drawable/ic_shortcut_capture"
        android:shortcutId="quick_capture"
        android:shortcutLongLabel="@string/shortcut_capture_long"
        android:shortcutShortLabel="@string/shortcut_capture_short">
        <intent
            android:action="com.kamsiob.claritynow.action.CAPTURE_UNFILED"
            android:targetClass="com.kamsiob.claritynow.MainActivity"
            android:targetPackage="@string/clarity_application_id" />
    </shortcut>

    <shortcut
        android:enabled="true"
        android:icon="@drawable/ic_shortcut_focus"
        android:shortcutId="start_focus"
        android:shortcutLongLabel="@string/shortcut_focus_long"
        android:shortcutShortLabel="@string/shortcut_focus_short">
        <intent
            android:action="com.kamsiob.claritynow.action.OPEN_FOCUS"
            android:targetClass="com.kamsiob.claritynow.MainActivity"
            android:targetPackage="@string/clarity_application_id" />
    </shortcut>

    <shortcut
        android:enabled="true"
        android:icon="@drawable/ic_shortcut_pulse"
        android:shortcutId="todays_pulse"
        android:shortcutLongLabel="@string/shortcut_pulse_long"
        android:shortcutShortLabel="@string/shortcut_pulse_short">
        <intent
            android:action="com.kamsiob.claritynow.action.OPEN_PULSE"
            android:targetClass="com.kamsiob.claritynow.MainActivity"
            android:targetPackage="@string/clarity_application_id" />
    </shortcut>
</shortcuts>
